## Governing process

The `process:` line at the top of this file names the process document that
governs this project. When it is not `null`, follow that process's gates and
approvals instead of the generic spec-before-code gate of the
`graph-agents-cli-workflow` skill, and treat the generic gate as satisfied only
by that process's approvals. When it is `null`, the generic gate applies:
write `.graph-agents-cli-spec.md` and get it approved before writing code.

## The loop

1. Build in `{{cookiecutter.agent_directory}}/`. Tools live in `{{cookiecutter.agent_directory}}/tools/`; every tool module
   declares `PRODUCT_CALLS` (empty when it calls no product API) and reaches the
   product only through `{{cookiecutter.agent_directory}}/app_utils/product_client.py`.
2. Try it: `graph-agents-cli playground` (the app with `/playground`), or
   `graph-agents-cli run "prompt"`. `graph-agents-cli playground --graph` opens
   LangGraph Studio against the graph directly (bypasses the auth policy).
3. Write eval cases by hand in `tests/eval/datasets/`, then `graph-agents-cli eval run`
   until the gate passes. `eval compare` shows regressions; `eval analyze` clusters failures.
4. `uv run pytest tests/unit tests/integration` and `graph-agents-cli lint` before deploying.
5. `graph-agents-cli deploy --env dev` **only after the user approves it.**
   Staging and production go through the CI/CD path recorded in the manifest (`cd: {{cookiecutter.cd}}`).

## Commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `graph-agents-cli playground` | Run the app with reload and open the dev chat page |
| `graph-agents-cli run "prompt"` | One-shot chat (`--mode a2a` for the A2A path, `--url` for a deployed agent) |
| `uv run pytest tests/unit tests/integration` | Unit and integration tests (fake model, in-memory checkpointer) |
| `graph-agents-cli eval run` | Generate traces and grade them against the gate |
| `graph-agents-cli lint` | ruff plus the product-policy check of every tool |
| `graph-agents-cli build` | Build the container image from the runtime's Dockerfile |
| `graph-agents-cli deploy --env <env>` | Deploy (direct modes) or open the desired-state PR (argocd) |
| `graph-agents-cli secrets apply --env <env>` | Create or update the environment's app Secret from an env file |
| `graph-agents-cli infra check --env <env>` | Read-only report of cluster and GitHub prerequisites |

## Rules

- **Spec before code** unless the governing process says otherwise (see above).
- **Change only what was asked.** Preserve surrounding code, comments, config values and formatting.
- **Never change the model** (`MODEL_PROVIDER`, `MODEL_NAME`) unless explicitly asked.
  A model 404 means the name is wrong for the provider or the endpoint; fix the
  configuration in `.env`, not `{{cookiecutter.agent_directory}}/agent.py`.
- **Human approval before deploy.** Never run `graph-agents-cli deploy` without the user's explicit go-ahead.
- **Run Python through uv**: `uv run python script.py`, after `uv sync`.
- **Three strikes.** The same error three times means fix the cause, not retry.
- **Tools declare their product calls.** Add `PRODUCT_CALLS` entries for every
  product API call a tool makes; `graph-agents-cli lint` refuses undeclared or
  disallowed calls. Never bypass `product_client.py` with a raw HTTP client.
- **Never edit `product-policy.yaml`, `graph-agents-cli-manifest.yaml` or
  `values-prod.yaml`** unless the user asks; production desired state changes only
  through a pull request reviewed by the code owners.
- **Do not export prompts or user data** to a hosted tracing destination unless
  the user has decided so (`TRACING_ENABLED`, `TRACE_CAPTURE=full`).
